But yeah, the key here is that the server gives the session a UUID as a session ID and then the client refers to that using an HTTP header to make sure that the server and client both understand the ongoing context.
That's really it.
The idea of SSEs still happens inside of this, but it's only part of the architecture instead of all of it.
We're going to implement our MCP main.js again but instead in `streamable.js` and using Express as our Node.js server.
Express is chosen because we really just need minimal HTTP helpers and it's the one everyone gets.
You can use Fastify, Next.js or whatever you want here.
